  "scope": "Isolated D284 two independently refillable exact query contexts per worker, ceil(requested_threads/2) query workers, original requested graph-loader count. At default12 there remain12 query contexts/maps but6 OS query threads. Stage both contexts CSR-prefix prefetch, then range/adjacency prefetch, then complete original32-item relaxation batches; termination only between complete context batches, exact labels/heaps/best isolated. Completed/skipped contexts refill immediately, every query output owns its original atomic index. No cached answers/query dedup, no graph/seed/geometry assumptions. This is coarse query interleaving inspired by AMAC independent/refillable-state principle, not a complete AMAC implementation or a claimed speedup. Header algorithms/32-band batches/full64/wide weights/parse/build/PGO unchanged. Native screen only; fresh state/ownership/refill/odd/empty/zero/long/Floyd/strict/race/GCC/image/default/actual proof required if useful.",
